ducation Collection Development Policy Library Hours Connect With Us Email Us (Ask a Librarian) Facebook Call Us FAQs Your Feedback Take a Survey Patron’s Voice Library Resources Find Library Catalog Ebooks Journal Articles Theses & Dissertations Course Guides AIIAS Repository Open Access Databases Explore Special Collections Adventist Sources AIIAS Publications Linkages Experience Apps & Tools LLM & GenerativeAI Services & Spaces Services For Campus Students Online, Extension & Cohort Faculty Staff Alumni Visitors Borrowing How to Borrow? Renew Books Reserve Books Things for Loan Interlibrary Loan Request an Article/Book Chapter Library Spaces Learning Commons EGW Branch Office Asian Studies Center Study Cubicles/Carrels Classroom Teaching & Tutorials Classroom Instructions One-on-One Tutorials Library Seminars & Workshops Research Help Research Skills Information Literacy Learning Search Strategies GenerativeAI in Research Evaluating Sources Evaluating Online Resources Misinformation & Fake News Responsible Use of GenAI Citations APA Style SBL Style AIIAS Writing Manuals Zotero Research submission AIIAS Repository Submission ProQuest Submission Submission and Clearance Requirements Visitors Services For Campus Students Online, Extension & Cohort Faculty Staff Alumni Visitors The Leslie Hardinge Library is open to all individuals who are seeking for spiritual growth and knowledge from the vast pool of information available in the collection. How do you benefit from this service? Present your valid school/organization ID and referral letter from your librarian to the security guard on duty at AIIAS main gate. The guard will give you a visitor’s pass in exchange of your ID. He will also instruct you on the way to the library. At the library counter, present your visitor’s pass and give the referral letter. You must also pay Php50 as a library fee and read and sign an agreement form. The personnel will also give you the visiting researcher’s ID. You need to wear the ID during your stay in the library. The researchers need to abide by the policies of the library and the Philippine Copyright Law. The library is open to visiting researchers from Monday to Thursday, 8:00 AM-5:00 PM only. Services for Visiting Researchers: Library Access – Visiting researchers may use the library’s study areas and reference collections during operating hours. Research Assistance – Our librarians can assist with research inquiries, resource navigation, and citation guidance. Electronic Resources – Access to selected online databases and digital collections is available within the library premises. Document Delivery – Limited photocopying and printing services are available for academic use, in compliance with copyright policies. Workspaces – Quiet study spaces and research desks are provided for focused academic work. Note: Borrowing privileges are generally limited to AIIAS students and faculty. Visiting researchers are encouraged to consult a library staff regarding access to specific materials. For further details, please visit the library’s information desk or contact us at ask.a.librarian@aiias.edu . Library Hours Sunday: 8:00 am – 8:00 pm Monday: 7:30 am – 9:30 pm Tuesday: 7:30 am – 9:30 pm Wednesday: 7:30 am – 6:00 pm Thursday: 7:30 am – 9:30 pm Friday: 7:30 am – 12:00 pm Holidays: 8:00 am – 4:00 pm Quick Links FAQs Staff Directory Tutorials Visitors Library Forms Classic Portal AIIAS Homepage FAQs Staff Directory Tutorials Visitors Library Forms Classic Portal AIIAS Homepage Contact Us Adventist International Institute of Advanced Studies Aguinaldo Highway, Km. 45.5, Lalaan I, Silang, Cavite 4118, Philippines +63 46 4144 400 © 2025 Leslie Hardinge Library. All Rights Reserved. Search",
